WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Imagine trying to pay for
lunch with a bag of apples.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.960
The café would have to want apples,

3
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.850
and want them right now.

4
00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:11.670
Economists call this the
double coincidence of wants.

5
00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.410
Now hand over a slip of
printed paper with almost

6
00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.390
no value as an object.

7
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.300
The café takes it happily.

8
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.830
So why will a shop swap
a meal for a printed

9
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.050
slip of paper but not for a bag of apples?

10
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.760
In this mission, you'll uncover
the four jobs that money does,

11
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.290
and what happens when it stops doing them.

12
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.590
Then you'll rank assets on a ladder,

13
00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.330
from notes and coins down to houses.

14
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:39.000
Your mission: find out what
turns something into money.
